e 250 m match radius, at 08:12:50 and 08:19:40 within the trace window. Because the deviation is exonerated as an external event, POL-RD-09(2) refunds off-route ERP to the rider as a standalone pass-through correction, capped at SGD 12.00; SGD 4.00 is well within the cap. This is the rider's recovery, and it is not added to any distance refund — there is none — so there is no double counting under POL-RD-09(1).\n\nDRIVER ADVOCATE'S CLAIMS. Accepted: that POL-RD-03 fully exonerates the excess (cap 4.12 km, measured 2.98 km); that all three POL-RD-03 conditions are met; that POL-RD-02 does not run against the rider and no distance refund is owed; that the rider's recovery is the off-route ERP pass-through under POL-RD-09(2); that neither ERP line is phantom, so POL-RD-09(4) adds nothing and produces no billing-integrity referral; that no POL-RD-06 repeat-deviation pattern exists (deviation_flags_90d 0 against completed_trips_90d 553, and the deviation is not material) so neither the FULL_REFUND uplift nor a conduct referral follows; that the trace is unimpaired under POL-RD-07 (175 fixes, 10.0 s interval, 100% coverage, no gaps, max_gap_sec 0.0), closing the POL-RD-10(3) escalation ground; and that the chat shows the diversion was the driver's response to the closure with rider notice. The driver's alternative figure of SGD 4.15 is not used: it comes from running POL-RD-02 against a closure-adjusted optimal, which POL-RD-03 directs only where excess survives the cap — here none does, so the correct pass-through figure is SGD 4.00.\n\nRIDER ADVOCATE'S CLAIMS. Accepted: that a deviation is established on the trace figure 11.18 km (not the rounded 11.2 km convenience copy); that the booked route carries no ERP of its own; that both charged gantries are off-optimal and genuinely crossed; that the closure exonerates only the driver's distance and time conduct and does not shift government-set pass-through onto the rider, so POL-RD-09(2) returns the SGD 4.00; that POL-RD-04